@startuml processing
title Radar V1 module responsibilities and confirmed ordering
top to bottom direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

legend right
Green: bounded WP4/G2 implementation evidence only.
Yellow: confirmed responsibility; complete implementation not established.
Red: method or relative ordering remains open.
endlegend

component "ADC samples\nDUT input" as ADC #FFF2CC
component "Digital downconversion\nDDC; continuous stream state" as DDC #B7E1CD
component "Azimuth beamforming\ncommanded look; V1 reports\ncommanded azimuth" as BF #B7E1CD
component "Range processing" as RANGE #FFF2CC
component "Pulse accumulation +\nrange-migration handling\nInitial baseline: accumulate / prepare;\nno compensation" as ACC #FFF2CC
component "Doppler processing" as DOP #FFF2CC

ADC --> DDC
DDC --> BF
BF --> RANGE
RANGE --> ACC
ACC --> DOP

package "Additional approved responsibilities; relative ordering open" {
  component "Range-ambiguity handling\nMethod open; retain 100 km" as RA #F4CCCC
  component "Doppler unfolding\nSeparate module; method / order open" as UNFOLD #F4CCCC
  component "CFAR" as CFAR #FFF2CC
  component "Multi-PRF fusion\n3-of-5 baseline" as FUSE #B7E1CD
  component "Clustering" as CLUST #B7E1CD
  component "Elevation estimation\nFour complex elevation inputs from selected\nrange-Doppler candidates; angle +\nquality/validity outputs" as ELEV #FFF2CC
  component "Detection reporting" as REPORT #FFF2CC
  RA -[hidden]right- UNFOLD
  UNFOLD -[hidden]right- ELEV
  RA -[hidden]down- CFAR
  DOP -[hidden]right- RA
}

CFAR --> FUSE : accepted post-CFAR order
FUSE --> CLUST : accepted post-CFAR order
CLUST --> REPORT : reporting follows clustering

note bottom of ACC
Truth-assisted compensation is permitted only as a test/oracle comparison.
Scenario truth is never a production DUT input. Whether later compensation
is required, its method, and any feedback dependencies remain open.
end note
@enduml
